                                <div id="divFactoringFirstClaim">
                                    <p style="font-size: 13px; text-align: justify;">
                                        We (the MLI) certify that:
                                     <br />
                                        <br />
                                        1.	The information provided in the uploaded file (Called the Claim File) is true & correct and comply with 
                                            <br />
                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  Credit Guarantee Fund Scheme for Factoring (CGFSF) as notified in the Gazette Notification  
                                            <br />
                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; dated September 22, 2015.
                                            <br />
                                        <br />
                                        2.  Claim for each Factored debt included in the File has been lodged with the guarantor as per extant   
                                            <br />
                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  CGFSF Gazette Notification.
                                            <br />
                                        <br />
                                        3.  All the recoveries pertaining to each factored debt after the date of NPA and before the claim 
                                            <br />
                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  lodgment have been duly incorporated in the Continuity File.
                                            <br />
                                        <br />
                                        4.	No deficiencies have been pointed out by Internal or External Auditors or other agencies in matter of   
                                            <br />
                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; appraisal/renewal/follow-up/conduct of the account included in the claim file.
                                            <br />
                                        <br />
                                        5.	Claims have been lodged only for the Assigned Factored Debts.
                                            <br />
                                        <br />
                                        6.	The proposal for factoring is in accordance with the extant rules and regulations and conduct the 
                                            <br />
                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  account(s) of the borrowers with normal factoring practices/financial prudence. 
                                            <br />
                                        <br />
                                        7.	We shall ensure to submit the information required by NCGTC for giving guarantee cover with regard to 
                                            <br />
                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  factored debt within 3 days from the date of the first operation in the account.
                                            <br />
                                        <br />
                                        8.	We shall ensure that the guarantee claim in respect of the factored debt and borrower is lodged with  
                                            <br />
                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  NCGTC after a period of 90 days but within 120 days from date of account turning NPA,in  
                                            <br />
                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  form and in the manner in this behalf and that there is no delay on our part to notify the
                                            <br />
                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  default in borrowers account which shall result in the Fund facing higher guarantee claims. 
                                            <br />
                                        <br />
                                        9.	The payment of guarantee claim by NCGTC to the does not in any way take away the responsibility of 
                                            <br />
                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  the Factor to recover entire outstanding amount of factored debt given with recourse,from   
                                            <br />
                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  borrower with applicable interest. Factor shall exercise all necessary precautions and initiate 
                                              <br />
                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  necessary actions for recovery of outstanding amount,including such action as advised by NCGTC.  
                                            <br />
                                        <br />
                                        10.	Factor shall comply with such directions as may be issued by NCGTC, from time to time, for facilitating  
                                            <br />
                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  recoveries in guaranteed account, or safeguarding its interest as a credit guarantor, 
                                            <br />
                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  as NCGTC may deem fit and the factor shall be bound to comply with such directions.
                                            <br />
                                        <br />
                                        11.	The Factor shall, in respect of any guaranteed account, exercise the same diligence in recovering the
                                            <br />
                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  dues,safeguarding interest of the fund in all the ways open to it as it might have exercised  
                                            <br />
                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  in normal course if no guarantee had been furnished by the Fund. The Factor shall,in particular, 
                                             <br />
                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  refrain from any act of omission or commission, either before or subsequent to invocation of 
                                             <br />
                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  guarantee,which may adversely affect the interest of the Fund as the guarantor. 
                                            <br />
                                        <br />
                                        12.	Post invocation of the guarantee claim, if any recoveries are made, the recoveries shall first be 
                                            <br />
                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  adjusted towards legal costs for recovery of the amount and then shall share proportionately  
                                            <br />
                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  the recoveries affected in an account, upto the extent of amount of claim settled by NCGTC.
                                            <br />
                                        <br />
                                        13.	If any amount due to NCGTC remains unpaid beyond a period of 30 days from the date on which it was  
                                            <br />
                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  first recovered,interest shall be payable to NCGTC at the rate which is 4% above Bank Rate  
                                            <br />
                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  for the period for which payment remains outstanding after expiry of said period of 30 days.
                                            <br />
                                        <br />
                                        14.	In case any of the information provided by us is found to be incorrect, the guarantee cover provided 
                                            <br />
                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  by NCGTC under CGFSF shall become Null & Void.
                                            <br />
                                        <br />


                                    </p>

